# What NOT to sync into the workspace.
#
# The inverse of the other bundle types': for them dist/ is build junk, here it
# is the ENTIRE payload. The deployed app is dist/ + server.mjs + app.yml and
# nothing else — no node_modules, no TypeScript, no test files. server.mjs has
# no dependencies precisely so this stays true.
#
# If you add a runtime dependency to server.mjs you must also stop ignoring
# node_modules, and the deploy grows from kilobytes to tens of megabytes. That
# is the trade being made here; make it deliberately.

node_modules/
.npm/
src/
public/
scripts/
docs/
test/
coverage/

*.ts
*.tsx
*.test.*
tsconfig*.json
vite.config.*
eslint.config.*
components.json
.prettierrc.json
.prettierignore
.nvmrc
index.html
package-lock.json

.git/
.gitlab-ci.yml
.idea/
.vscode/
.databricks/
.vite/
CONFIG.md
*.log
